I have just realized something with the library matching. This chunk of code check the list of tags and check if all the tags in a given line are provided by the OS, and if so, it returns the first matching library:
```
	if (p_config->has_section("libraries")) {
		List<String> libraries;
		p_config->get_section_keys("libraries", &libraries);

		for (const String &E : libraries) {
			Vector<String> tags = E.split(".");
			bool all_tags_met = true;
			for (int i = 0; i < tags.size(); i++) {
				String tag = tags[i].strip_edges();
				if (!p_has_feature(tag)) {
					all_tags_met = false;
					break;
				}
			}

			if (all_tags_met) {
				String library_path = p_config->get_value("libraries", E);
				if (library_path.is_relative_path()) {
					library_path = p_path.get_base_dir().path_join(library_path);
				}
				if (r_tags != nullptr) {
					r_tags->append_array(tags);
				}
				return library_path;
			}
		}
	}
```
That may cause the following configuration to select the first library to be selected instead of the second one:
```
[libraries]

windows = "bin/windows.dll"
windows.debug = "bin/windows.debug.dll"
```
Maybe I should implement the same "return the most matching lib" behavior I implemented for the autodetection ?
